Locality-Sensitive Hashing","author":"Koga, Hisashi and Ishibashi, Tetsuo and Watanabe, Toshinori","journal":"Knowledge and Information Systems","volume":"12","number":"1","pages":"25--53","year":"2007","publisher":"Springer"},"diffs":[{"field":"year","in_document":"2007","in_source":"2006","severity":"medium"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"kolda2009tensor","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"a13f3887c5e16a64","fields":{"title":"Tensor decompositions and applications","author":"Kolda, Tamara G and Bader, Brett W","journal":"SIAM review","volume":"51","number":"3","pages":"455--500","year":"2009","publisher":"SIAM"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"koldaBader","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"8fd16d0a16d4c75f","fields":{"author":"Kolda, Tamara G. and Bader, Brett W.","title":"Tensor Decompositions and Applications","journal":"SIAM Review","volume":"51","number":"3","pages":"455-500","year":"2009","doi":"10.1137/07070111X","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/07070111X","eprint":"https://doi.org/10.1137/07070111X","abstract":"This survey provides an overview of higher-order tensor decompositions, their applications, and available software. A tensor is a multidimensional or N-way array. Decompositions of higher-order tensors (i.e., N-way arrays with \\$N \\geq 3\\$) have applications in psycho-metrics, chemometrics, signal processing, numerical linear algebra, computer vision, numerical analysis, data mining, neuroscience, graph analysis, and elsewhere. Two particular tensor decompositions can be considered to be higher-order extensions of the matrix singular value decomposition: CANDECOMP/PARAFAC (CP) decomposes a tensor as a sum of rank-one tensors, and the Tucker decomposition is a higher-order form of principal component analysis. There are many other tensor decompositions, including INDSCAL, PARAFAC2, CANDELINC, DEDICOM, and PARATUCK2 as well as nonnegative variants of all of the above. The N-way Toolbox, Tensor Toolbox, and Multilinear Engine are examples of software packages for working with tensors."},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"kulis2009kernelized","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"110410dd20e742dd","fields":{"title":"Kernelized locality-sensitive hashing for scalable image search","author":"Kulis, Brian and Grauman, Kristen","booktitle":"2009 IEEE 12th international conference on computer vision","pages":"2130--2137","year":"2009","organization":"IEEE"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"li2006very","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"b56f4c061d46b69f","fields":{"title":"Very sparse random projections","author":"Li, Ping and Hastie, Trevor J and Church, Kenneth W","booktitle":"Proceedings of the 12th ACM SIGKDD international conference on Knowledge discovery and data mining","pages":"287--296","year":"2006"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"liao2013depression","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"0bfe0ef2e19c7200","fields":{"title":"Is depression a disconnection syndrome? Meta-analysis of diffusion tensor imaging studies in patients with MDD","author":"Liao, Yi and Huang, Xiaoqi and Wu, Qizhu and Yang, Chuang and Kuang, Weihong and Du, Mingying and Lui, Su and Yue, Qiang and Chan, Raymond CK and Kemp, Graham J and others","journal":"Journal of Psychiatry and Neuroscience","volume":"38","number":"1","pages":"49--56","year":"2013","publisher":"Journal of Psychiatry and Neuroscience"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"mori2006principles","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:44:41Z","response_hash":"ed8205405af5910a","fields":{"title":"Principles of diffusion tensor imaging and its applications to basic neuroscience research","autho